import ../../../ui/scene_uploads.dl
import ../../../ui/scene_surfaces.dl

class:
    patterns:
        scene upload recorder
    members:
        vertices as an integer
        indices as an integer
        draws as an integer

to get [the scene upload recorder in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    return view's instance's state as a pointer to scene upload recorder

to [record scene vertices in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [slot] {integer:slot} [from] {a pointer:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    require condition ((shader = (321 as a pointer)) and (pass = 3)) reporting "Scene uploads changed their shader or pass"
    require condition (0 <= slot <= 2) reporting "Scene uploads used an unknown stream"
    if slot = 2:
        require condition (count = 176) reporting "Scene instance uploads must use the portable record stride"
        set record to the value at (data as a pointer to UI scene shader instance)
        require condition ((the item at 0 in record's matrix) = 1.0) reporting "Instance bytes were corrupted at the driver boundary"
    else:
        set stride to 32 if slot = 0, else 12
        require condition ((count = (24 * stride)) or (count = (48 * stride))) reporting "Scene geometry bytes disagree with their vertex layouts"
    increment (the scene upload recorder in view)'s vertices

to [record scene indices in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [from] {a pointer to a 32 bit unsigned integer:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    require condition ((count = 36) or (count = 72)) reporting "Scene index uploads changed their count"
    increment (the scene upload recorder in view)'s indices

to [record scene draws in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [from] {a pointer to UI shader draw:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    set draw to the value at data
    require condition ((count = 1) and ((draw's count = 36) and ((draw's first = 36) and ((draw's vertex offset = 24) and ((draw's instances = 2) and (draw's instance offset = 7)))))) reporting "Scene draws did not preserve mesh-local indices and instance offsets"
    increment (the scene upload recorder in view)'s draws

set operations to a new UI shader operations
set operations' vertices to (the function named "record scene vertices in $ holding $ pass $ slot $ from $ counting $") as a pointer
set operations' indices to (the function named "record scene indices in $ holding $ pass $ from $ counting $") as a pointer
set operations' draws to (the function named "record scene draws in $ holding $ pass $ from $ counting $") as a pointer
set driver to a new UI driver
set driver's shader operations to the address of operations
set recorder to a new scene upload recorder
set instance to a new UI instance
set instance's state to (the address of recorder) as a pointer
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set view's driver to the address of driver
set bank to a UI scene mesh bank
set mesh to a UI box mesh with 1 by 1 by 1 segments
set first to the span of UI mesh mesh in bank
set binding to a UI scene geometry binding to bank in (the address of view) shader (321 as a pointer) pass 3
require condition (refresh UI scene geometry binding (the address of binding)) reporting "The first scene geometry upload was omitted"
require condition ((refresh UI scene geometry binding (the address of binding)) = false) reporting "Unchanged scene geometry was uploaded again"
set second to the span of UI mesh (a UI box mesh with 1 by 1 by 1 segments) in bank
require condition (refresh UI scene geometry binding (the address of binding)) reporting "New scene geometry was not uploaded"
require condition (((recorder's vertices = 4) and (recorder's indices = 2)) and (binding's revision = 2)) reporting "Scene geometry revision tracking lost or repeated uploads"
set records to an empty list of UI scene shader instance
set material to a UI scene material with color (UI ink 255 255 255) roughness 0.5 metalness 0.0
append (a UI scene shader instance through (a UI scene transform from (an identity graphics matrix)) with material material casting shadow true receiving shadow true) to records
upload UI scene instances records through binding
set draw to a UI scene mesh draw from span second in bank counting 2 instances starting at 7
set UI shader (binding's shader) pass (binding's pass) in (binding's view) to draws (the address of draw) counting 1
require condition ((recorder's vertices = 5) and (recorder's draws = 1)) reporting "Dynamic scene instances or draws did not reach the driver"
free records
close UI scene mesh bank bank
print line "Scene uploads retain static geometry across frames and transfer portable instance records and indexed draws."
